This project implements ideas from the following published work. The
implementation is independent; no upstream source code was copied.

  McFarland, T., Bellavita, J., & Guidi, G. (2025).
  "Parallel GPU-Enabled Algorithms for SpGEMM on Arbitrary Semirings with
  Hybrid Communication." ICPE '25. doi:10.1145/3676151.3719365
  -- Cornell University

  Chen, C., Kuncham, G., Subramoni, H., & Panda, D. K. (2025).
  "Design and Implementation of a GPU-Aware MPI Collective Library for Intel
  GPUs." ISC High Performance 2025.
  -- The Ohio State University

  Chen, C., Kuncham, G., Subramoni, H., & Panda, D. K. (2024).
  "Design and Implementation of Kernel-based MPI Reduction Operations for Intel
  GPUs." 31st IEEE International Conference on High Performance Computing,
  Data, and Analytics (HPDC).
  -- The Ohio State University

  Ivanov, A., Shen, S., Gottardo, G., Chrapek, M., Boudaoud, A., Schneider, T.,
  Benini, L., & Hoefler, T. (2025).
  "PerfDojo: Automated ML Library Generation for Heterogeneous Architectures."
  SC '25.
  -- ETH Zurich

  Montoya, S., Muino, G., Lee, A., Oberg, L., Wood, E., McJohn, M., Zhang, L.,
  Kumar, S., Song, Z., Bhalerao, A., Zhou, M., et al. (2024).
  "Overview of the LAMMPS HPC Benchmark Suite."
  -- Sandia National Laboratories / LBNL / UT Austin

  Buluç, A., & Gilbert, J. R. (2011).
  "Sparse Matrix-Matrix Multiplication is Almost Always of the Form..."
  / "Parallel Sparse Matrix-Matrix Multiplication on Scalable Multiprocessors."
  -- University of California, Berkeley

  Zwick, U. (2002). "All Pairs Shortest Paths via Multiple Matrix Multiplication."
  -- Weizmann Institute of Science

  Chakradhar, S., et al.; Trilinos / CombBLAS design lineage.
  -- Sandia National Laboratories

The specific hybrid-communication heuristic (direct device-to-device for
small messages, host-staged for large ones) follows the empirical finding
reported in McFarland, Bellavita & Guidi (ICPE 2025). The Crossover points are
measured, not assumed: `benchmarks/comm_microbench.cpp` measures them on the
target fabric and `HybridCommunicator::autotune_thresholds()` applies the
result.
